michelle (CSM): Quick weekly check-in for Lumina Health — error surface for the last 7d. High-level: 5xx rate up to 1.8% (↑ vs last week), timeouts ~0.9% (slightly down), rate-limit hits ~0.6% (↑ during nightly windows). Top failing endpoints by error-volume: 1) /v1/generate — majority 5xx spikes; 2) /v1/embed — timeouts on large batch calls; 3) /v1/chat/stream — bursts hitting rate limits. Can we triage root causes and propose mitigations?

josh (SRE): On it. Can you drop the Lumina account id and a couple sample request IDs from the timeframe? Also what's p95 for /v1/generate vs last week?

michelle (CSM): Account: lumina-001. Sample req ids: r_abc123, r_def456, r_ghi789. p95 for /v1/generate last week ~220ms, current p95 ~360ms (observed during 02:00-04:00 UTC nightly syncs).

anita (AE): Lumina mentioned they rolled SDK v2.1.3 last Tuesday and started sending larger batch embed jobs overnight. They said retry settings are default.

kai (eng-runtime): Quick findings from infra logs: seeing repeated `Timeout waiting for KV-cache lock` on model replica model-a-3 around those req ids. Also a pattern of concurrent large batch embed jobs + chat streams causing KV cache thrash and raising token latency; that leads to upstream 5xx (internal timeouts) and client retry storms that push them into rate limits.

josh (SRE): Logs snippet for r_abc123: ```
2026-03-19T02:14:12Z model-a-3 ERROR Timeout while waiting for kv-cache lock (waited 120s) trace=r_abc123
2026-03-19T02:14:12Z proxy WARN upstream response 524 for /v1/generate req=r_abc123
```

kai (eng-runtime): Two immediate mitigations we can do: 1) temporary per-account burst allowance for lumina-001 for next 24h to avoid rate-limit fallout; 2) route Lumina's /v1/embed batch jobs to a less-loaded quantized model variant until KV-cache patch is deployed. Longer term: increase KV lock concurrency and add per-route token reservations for large batches.

michelle (CSM): Proposed action items: - Ops: add a 24h burst whitelist for lumina-001 and increase per-route concurrency cap on /v1/embed. - Eng: investigate kv-cache contention and prepare a small fix (target patch + canary). - CS/AE: coordinate with Lumina on applying SDK backoff guidance and ask them to space batch windows if possible. I'll notify Lumina and offer the temporary whitelist.

anita (AE): I'll confirm Lumina's nightly schedule and ask them to apply exponential backoff (example below). Will also request they roll back to SDK v2.1.2 if issues persist.

kai (eng-runtime): Backoff snippet we can share: ```js
// recommended simple exponential backoff for SDK calls
async function callWithBackoff(fn, retries=4) {
  for (let i=0;i<retries;i++){
    try { return await fn(); } catch(e) {
      const delay = Math.min(1000 * Math.pow(2,i), 10000);
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, delay));
    }
  }
  throw new Error('max retries exceeded');
}
```

josh (SRE): Ops command to add temporary burst (internal only): ```
# grant lumina-001 +20% burst allowance for 24h
redwoodctl accounts update lumina-001 --burst-add 20 --burst-ttl 24h
```

deploy-bot: Deploy queued: `kv-cache-lock-fix` -> staging canary (will run 10% traffic) :hourglass_flowing_sand:

michelle (CSM): Thanks team — can we aim for patch canary today and ops change now? I'll update Lumina with the temporary whitelist + backoff snippet and set expectation for follow-up tomorrow. :thumbsup:
